  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 4: THE CAGE"
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt lay on the cold stone, the ghost of the severed connection a bleeding wound in his psyche."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator in his mind was a silent, shuddering thing."
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "Kethran found them there."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "The young Solantri scholar looked from the dark pool to Geralt, his luminous eyes full of a grief too deep for his years. “He saved you."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "He saved us all.”"
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "“At what cost?” Oreck rumbled, helping Geralt to his feet."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "“The spire is orphaned,” Luminaire confirmed, her voice heavy. “Umbrageous is stable, but dormant."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "Network resonance is dropping… 55% to 47%."
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "The cascade is slowed."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "But Geralt, your applicator remains."
  - line: 193
    type: narration
    text: "The architecture the network used is still there."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "It is a door they can try to open again.”"
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt touched his temple, feeling the fragile, wounded presence within."
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "It wasn’t the network."
  - line: 198
    type: narration
    text: "It was his."
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "And it was terrified."
  - line: 201
    type: narration
    text: "“We cage it,” he said, his voice raw."
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "Kethran nodded. “A harmonic isolation barrier."
  - line: 204
    type: narration
    text: "We Solantri are made of remembered light."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "We can weave a prison of specific frequencies around its core processes."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "It will be able to function for you—calculation, interface, armor control."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "But it will be deaf and mute to any external signals."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "It will be alone.”"
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "Alone."
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "The thought sent a pang through Geralt."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "After everything, to condemn it to solitude…"
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "A weak pulse echoed in his mind."
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "Not a word."
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "A feeling."
  - line: 217
    type: narration
    text: "Agreement."
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "Safety."
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator preferred the silence of a cage to the noise of its chains."
  - line: 221
    type: narration
    text: "“Do it,” Geralt said."
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "The procedure was not physical."
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "Kethran placed his hands on Geralt’s head, and his nacreous skin began to glow."
  - line: 225
    type: narration
    text: "A complex, haunting harmony filled the air, weaving into a lattice of pure sound."
  - line: 226
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt it pass through his skull, not as pain, but as a profound pressure, a tightening."
  - line: 228
    type: narration
    text: "He felt the Applicator’s presence shrink, drawing in on itself as the harmonic cage solidified around its core."
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "The constant, low-level awareness of its processes faded to a faint hum."
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "The open channel where the network had forced its way in was sealed, welded shut by layers of resonant light."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "It was done."
  - line: 234
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt opened his eyes."
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "The world was the same, and utterly different."
  - line: 236
    type: narration
    text: "The voice in his head, the partner he had argued with, negotiated with, relied upon for eight years… was quiet."
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "Muffled."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "Isolated."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "He was alone in his own skull in a way he hadn’t been since the mines."
  - line: 242
    type: narration
    text: "“It is isolated,” Kethran confirmed, stepping back, his light dimmed from the effort. “The cage will hold unless subjected to psychic force of a magnitude that would likely kill you first.”"
  - line: 244
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt flexed his hand."
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon armor responded, plates shifting smoothly."
  - line: 246
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator still worked."
  - line: 247
    type: narration
    text: "It was just… locked in."
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "A tool again, in the most literal sense."
  - line: 249
    type: narration
    text: "The partnership was not broken, but it had been placed behind soundproof glass."
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck clasped his shoulder. “You all right?”"
  - line: 253
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt met his friend’s gaze. “I will be.” He looked at the dark Pool, at the lost Keeper, at the saved and broken creatures they had left behind. “We stopped it."
  - line: 254
    type: narration
    text: "But they showed us our weakness.”"
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh materialized beside them, his expression grim. “The enemy knows how to hurt you now."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "Not with blades, but with your own history.”"
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s presence was a grim whisper. “The network resonance is stable for now."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "But two spires remain: the Shattered Mind, and the Ghost Spire itself."
  - line: 261
    type: narration
    text: "The Queen’s gaze is upon us."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "And she has just learned that the Anchor can be hijacked.”"
  - line: 264
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood in the darkness of the orphaned spire, the silence in his head a new kind of burden."
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "The victory tasted of ash and sacrifice."
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "They had survived the enemy within."
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "But the war for the network was just beginning, and he would now have to fight the rest of it with a vital part of himself locked in a cage of his own making."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 053-the twilight city"

